+HARDENING ACTIONS - SUMMARY
+
+This patch implements:
+- Sandbox hardening: RuntimeClass (kata), seccomp, AppArmor templates, NetworkPolicy, pod-executor deployment and RBAC.
+- Image supply chain: cosign image-signature webhook, cosign-key secret template, CI pre-check workflow to refuse unsigned images.
+- Verifier calibration: calculate_thresholds.py and periodic calibration workflow (weekly).
+- Retriever & Milvus ops: production Helm values, backup CronJob, backup helper script and restore-test job.
+- Webhook resilience: CA rotation script and a runbook for webhook outages, HA webhook deployment with probes and fail-open/fail-closed toggle.
+- Compliance automation: redaction checker and cronjob to run scheduled verification and report to MCP.
+
+Operator next steps (short):
+1. Install kata runtime on node pool, label nodes, and schedule sandbox pods there.
+2. Mount seccomp JSON and AppArmor profile on nodes; ensure Pod specs reference them.
+3. Populate kube-system/cosign-key with cosign public key or configure keyless trust.
+4. Build & push images (image-webhook, pod-executor, milvus-backup, redaction-checker).
+5. Deploy Milvus with values-production.yaml, configure S3 backups and run restore test.
+6. Provide labeled verifier CSV at services/verifier/calibration/labeled.csv and run calibration workflow.
+7. Wire Presidio and ensure redaction-check runs succeed.
